    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **262 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `telephoneDisplay` field so the API returns the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a new read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from this spec at build time), documenting the format: country code, a space, then the national digits grouped in threes (e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` plus a `formatTelephoneDisplay(owner)` default method that:\n   - splits the E.164 digits into a country-code segment (1 for NANP `+1`, 2 otherwise, e.g. `+61` \u2014 mirroring the country codes `toE164` normalises to) and the national number,\n   - joins `+<cc>` and the national digits grouped in threes with spaces,\n   - returns the stored value unchanged when it's `null` or not well-formed E.164, so it never fabricates a display for unexpected input.\n\nThe `telephone` field itself is untouched and remains raw E.164. The specified acceptance test (`+61412345678` / `+61 412 345 678`) and all existing tests pass.",
